      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does it also apply to human generated CLs? The reason why we started to notice the issue is that @rysk@google.com enabled deps checking only on our CI builders experimentaly. \nWe wanted to enable `fail-on-bad-deps` on CQ and all places. However, the overhead is substantial (e.g. +6mins to Linux CQ builds). \n\nIf we enable fail-on-bad-deps on agent builds, we probably should enable it on developer builds, too. Otherwise, developers can\u0027t reproduce it. \n\nDoes it make more sense to add an instruction about fail-on-bad-deps somewhere so that agents can verify their CLs with the feature when they think it\u0027s necessary?",
