      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T02:51:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e do you have a recommendation on how we enable fail-on-bad-deps on agent and/or developer builds?\n\nTo be honest, given the overhead involved, I’m not yet certain which approach is best.\nHowever, organizing and improving the documentation comes at little cost, so it seems worth a try.\n\nOn further reflection, I’m concerned that running conditional `fail-on-bad-deps` checks—such as those triggered by `gn` changes, header modifications, or `AGENT_GENERATED_CL`—could confuse developers if the process fails due to `fail-on-bad-deps` errors originating from other CLs.",
      "parentUuid": "44c4c7d2_2caf2d20",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "e9f2ff314dbc59e18f9678941f444c6efcda797f",
